nio: publish static personalities before the lockdown sweep

The only surviving nio_publish_static_personalities() call sits in
StartIOKitMatching(), which runs after the lockdown. But PE_lockdown_iokit()
runs its own matching sweep earlier, during the lockdown, and reads the
catalogue at that moment. The static NioUfs driver has no OSKext/Info.plist
to publish its personality, so that early sweep saw no UFS personality at
all: the driver was never matched, probe()/start() were never called, and
no UFS line ever reached the panel - which is exactly the "no change" the
last five rounds showed even though the driver, personality and probe=12
were all in the kernel.

Run 570's own analysis (nio-publish-personalities-before-lockdown.patch)
concluded that publication must happen in iokit_post_constructor_init,
long before the lockdown. That early call was later removed while the
matching was moved around; this patch restores it. The function's static
bool keeps publication to once, so the later call in StartIOKitMatching()
is harmless. Both sweeps now see the same catalogue.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
@@ -107,6 +107,14 @@ iokit_post_constructor_init(void)
 	assert( root );
 	IOService::initialize();
 	IOCatalogue::initialize();
+	/* nio: publish the static drivers' personalities here, before the
+	 * lockdown. PE_lockdown_iokit() runs its matching sweep before bsd_init()
+	 * and reads the catalogue as it is then; the only surviving call sat in
+	 * StartIOKitMatching(), which runs after the lockdown. So the lockdown
+	 * sweep never saw NioUfs (nor the platform expert), no driver attached,
+	 * and start() was never entered. Publishing here makes both sweeps see
+	 * the same catalogue; the static bool in the function makes it once. */
+	nio_publish_static_personalities();
 	IOStatistics::initialize();
 	OSKext::initialize();
 	IOUserClient::initialize();
